ollowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-25T15:56:10Z","updated_at":"2026-05-25T15:56:10Z","body":"I can see if I can test with Windows as well later and see if it happens\n\nMake sure that you use a release template when testing as it does *not* occur in debug builds at least on Linux (as opposed to not happening specifically in the editor)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4535547622/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4540954473","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119740#issuecomment-4540954473","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119740","id":4540954473,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDql3aQ","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-26T06:14:22Z","updated_at":"2026-05-26T06:14:22Z","body":"I changed the MRP's code slightly (I didn't upload new zip file). Now every other bullet frees itself after 10 frames and every other after 150 frames. The differences are:\n- after 10 frames the bullet is still inside the wall --> you get error messages\n- after 150 frame the bullet is no longer inside the wall -->  no error messages\n\nConsole output now:\n```\nBULLET HIT WALL!, delete when inside\nBULLET FREE\nERROR: Attempt to disconnect a nonexistent connection from 'StaticBody2D:<StaticBody2D#32715572594>'. Signal: 'tree_entered', callable: ''.\n   at: _disconnect (core/object/object.cpp:1643)\nERROR: Attempt to disconnect a nonexistent connection from 'StaticBody2D:<StaticBody2D#32715572594>'. Signal: 'tree_exiting', callable: ''.\n   at: _disconnect (core/object/object.cpp:1643)\nBULLET EXITED WALL BODY\nBULLET HIT WALL!, delete after exited\nBULLET EXITED WALL BODY\nBULLET FREE\n```\n\nThe 10 frame delay can also be replaced with an immediate `queue_free()`, the bullet is already inside the wall.\n\nSo it seems that although the error messages are about tree entered/exited signals, this bug might have something to do with body exited signal when the node is already queued to be freed.\n\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\n## !!!!  If you try this code with the MRP, also change the timer interval to e.g. 5 seconds.  !!!!\n## !!!!  Connect Area2D's body_exited signal to this code's _on_area_2d_body_exited !!!!\n\nstatic var counter := 0\nvar id: int\nvar deletion_delay := -1\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tcounter += 1\n\tid = counter\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta: float) -> void:\n\tposition.x += delta * 100\n\t\n\tif deletion_delay > 0:\n\t\tdeletion_delay -= 1\n\t\tif deletion_delay <= 0:\n\t\t\tprints(\"BULLET FREE\")\n\t\t\tqueue_free()\n\nfunc _on_area_2d_body_entered(_body: Node2D) -> void:\n\tif id % 2 == 0:\n\t\tprints(\"BULLET HIT WALL!, delete when inside\")\n\t\tdeletion_delay = 10\n\telse:\n\t\tprints(\"BULLET HIT WALL!, delete after exited\")\n\t\tdeletion_delay = 150\n\nfunc _on_area_2d_body_exited(body: Node2D) -> void:\n\tprints(\"BULLET EXITED WALL BODY\")\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4540954473/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]